# F´ Cursor rules

The canonical guidance for AI coding agents in this repository — including
Cursor — is the repo-root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Read it before
proposing any change.

Skills are listed in `AGENTS.md` §5 and live under
[`.agents/`](../../.agents/):

- [`.agents/code-review.md`](../../.agents/code-review.md) — reviewing C++ changes
- [`.agents/component-author.md`](../../.agents/component-author.md) — new components
- [`.agents/unit-test-author.md`](../../.agents/unit-test-author.md) — unit tests

Hard constraints (see `AGENTS.md` §8 for the full list):

- Never edit autocoder output (`build-artifacts/`, `*ComponentAc.{hpp,cpp}`,
  `*TesterBase.*`, `*GTestBase.*`). Re-run `fprime-util generate` and
  `fprime-util impl` instead.
- No exceptions, RTTI, STL, `std::string`, lambdas, dynamic allocation after
  init, `NULL`/`0` as null pointers, C-style casts, or `using namespace` in
  framework or component code.
- All code must remain C++14 compliant.
- Never bypass pre-commit hooks (`--no-verify`), never push to `devel` or
  `master`, never run `git add .`.

This file is intentionally a thin pointer so `AGENTS.md` remains the single
source of truth for every AI tool.
